            "confidence": "high",
            "summary": "The skill appears to be a genuine Paytm integration guide, but its sample backends could expose real merchant payment authority if deployed without added access controls.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "External transmission to Paytm is expected for this skill, but the samples handle customer contact/payment data and merchant signing authority. Callback URLs can be derived from untrusted Host/X-Forwarded headers or request bodies, and the Spring sample enables wildcard CORS, which is disproportionate for production payment endpoints.",
                "label": "Credentials",
                "name": "environment_proportionality",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The README provides standard, disclosed global skill installation paths for Claude and Codex, including cloning into a skills directory or using a skill installer. I found no hidden installer, startup hook, cron job, or remote payload execution.",
                "label": "Install Mechanism",
                "name": "install_mechanism",
                "rating": "note"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The skill repeatedly frames the reference backends as production-oriented and tells agents to copy their idempotency and webhook patterns, but it does not equally require caller authentication, resource ownership checks, rate limits, or callback-domain allowlisting. It also contains strict terminology rules and a minor subscription scope inconsistency, which are not malicious but show overbroad instruction scope.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
                "name": "instruction_scope",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The skill uses explicit cross-session installation only. Runtime state is bounded in-memory idempotency and webhook audit data; it is disclosed and not a system persistence mechanism, though webhook payload retention should be minimized or protected in real deployments.",
                "label": "Persistence & Privilege",
                "name": "persistence_privilege",
                "rating": "note"
